  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Generate a 3D model"
    },
    "description": "Make a game-ready, low-poly 3D model (GLB) with fal.ai (Tripo P1) and save it inside app/. Give a prompt (a picture is made first, then turned into the model) or an image (a web address, or a picture inside the project such as reference/picture-1.png). faces caps the face count (48 to 20000, default 3000): about 500-1500 for small props and pickups, 2000-5000 for weapons, furniture and vehicles, 6000-15000 for main characters; fewer faces run faster, so use the fewest that still look right. textured (default true) gives colours and surfaces. A textured model costs $0.50 plus $0.15 for the picture, counted against the project's asset budget; it takes a minute or two. Describe one original object per model; never ask for recognisable characters, logos or brand artwork. Returns where it was saved, the cost and the budget left.",
